# Cursor Rules — Berkah POS SaaS

- Before any code, schema, deployment, CI, or architecture-document change, read root `AGENTS.md` and follow its mandatory reading order.
- `docs/permanent/DOC_00_CANONICAL_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` owns only the canonical five-layer configuration behavior and 352-entry workbook contract.
- `docs/permanent/ADR-2026-10-17-OWNER-KVM2-LARAVEL-POSTGRESQL-NO-SUPABASE.md` is the current owner authority: Hostinger KVM2 + Coolify, Laravel/PHP 8.4, private PostgreSQL 17, isolated environments, a measured growth path and **no Supabase products or project access**. The earlier 2026-10-16 ADR remains historical where it conflicts. Current `main` still has `supabase_flutter` and no root Composer manifest/lockfile; that is an implementation gap, not permission to use Supabase.
- `docs/permanent/DOC_00_MASTER_ROADMAP.md` governs ordered phases; `DOC_12` and `DOC_13` are historical/business evidence only where superseded. Never use Supabase for a new runtime, tests, builds, CI or read-only source access.
- Canonical inheritance is `GLOBAL -> TEMPLATE -> TENANT -> SERVICE -> DEVICE`; exact workbook inventory is 352 entries (1 global + 3 templates + 100 tenants + 140 service entries + 108 devices).
- Separate current source, accepted target, branch implementation, exact-head CI, staging and production evidence. Retain old Supabase-related code, SQL and reports only as clearly classified archive/audit material. Do not access live Supabase projects, even read-only, and do not run `scripts/sync_excel_to_supabase.py`. See the latest owner ADR and `docs/reports/SOURCE_OF_TRUTH_ALIGNMENT_CORRECTION_2026-10-16.md`.
- Resolve one requested service at a time; never merge POS and Akuntansi rows.
- Keep the workbook as the source/export contract. The target Laravel importer maps its entries to normalized central tables; do not restore a generic Supabase `app_config(key, value JSONB)` runtime or the legacy `(device_id, key, value)` shape.
- Flutter runtime configuration and sync target the authenticated Laravel Central API, while SQLite local-first checkout/outbox remains mandatory.
- The shared application image serves standard tenants. Each tenant gets a distinct PostgreSQL database and restricted runtime role on one private PostgreSQL 17 service; a reviewed broker provisions these resources. Development/staging/production use distinct databases and secrets. Never use root/global DB credentials in tenant request handling.
- Admin/Central routes and tenant routes must be domain-scoped and independently authorized; a client-supplied tenant ID or Host header is not proof of access.
- Preserve offline idempotency, FEFO physical allocation vs FIFO financial costing, and accurate evidence reporting.
- Use branches and pull requests, never direct implementation pushes to `main`. Never force-push, erase `.git`, or delete existing files blindly.
- New workflows use GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-24.04`; deploy immutable images only after required checks pass.
- `scripts/sync_excel_to_supabase.py` is prohibited legacy mutation-capable code. Never run it and never give it credentials. Existing data may only be imported from an already available owner-controlled offline artifact outside Supabase; otherwise data continuity remains unverified.
- Report unexecuted tests as `NOT RUN / NOT VERIFIED`; source presence and docs do not prove green CI, tenant isolation, successful restore, or production readiness.
